"[Security][P0] Make CAPTCHA verification fail closed when provider is configured"
## Summary
CAPTCHA verification currently allows login when a provider is configured but the secret key is missing. This should fail closed.

## Why
This is a pre-public-release security blocker (P0) because CAPTCHA can be silently bypassed when misconfigured.

## Scope
- Update CAPTCHA verification flow to reject auth when provider != none and secret key is empty.
- Surface clear admin/operator error messaging for misconfiguration.
- Add guardrails so this cannot silently regress.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Login is blocked when CAPTCHA provider is enabled and secret is missing/invalid.
- User receives a generic auth failure message.
- Admin/system logs clearly indicate CAPTCHA misconfiguration.
- Behavior is covered by automated checks/tests where applicable.


"[Security][P0] Encrypt CAPTCHA secret at rest and stop echoing stored secret in admin UI"
## Summary
CAPTCHA secret is stored as plain text and rendered back in the admin form.

## Why
This is a pre-public-release security blocker (P0) due to secret exposure risk through DB dumps, screenshots, and UI leaks.

## Scope
- Encrypt CAPTCHA secret at rest.
- Do not pre-fill CAPTCHA secret field with stored value.
- Support "leave blank to keep current secret" behavior.
- Ensure decryption only happens server-side when needed.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Stored CAPTCHA secret is encrypted at rest.
- Admin UI never displays the current secret value.
- Updating unrelated security settings does not overwrite secret unless explicitly changed.
- Backward compatibility/migration path exists for existing installations.


"[Security][P1] Enforce non-empty SMTP encryption secret and migrate plaintext SMTP passwords"
## Summary
SMTP password encryption is optional today if SMTP secret is empty, allowing plaintext-at-rest credentials.

## Why
Public release readiness requires eliminating optional plaintext credential storage.

## Scope
- Enforce non-empty SMTP encryption secret at boot/config validation.
- Block saving SMTP credentials when encryption secret is missing.
- Provide migration path to re-encrypt existing stored SMTP passwords.

## Acceptance Criteria
- SMTP password cannot be stored plaintext in supported configurations.
- Existing plaintext values are migrated or explicitly flagged for admin remediation.
- Documentation updated with required secret setup and rotation guidance.


"[Security][P1] Redact sensitive SMTP debug logging and define production logging policy"
## Summary
SMTP debug logging can capture sensitive protocol/session details to local logs.

## Why
Before going public, logging must minimize sensitive data exposure risk.

## Scope
- Redact sensitive values in SMTP debug output.
- Restrict or disable verbose SMTP debug in production by default.
- Document safe operational guidance for temporary troubleshooting.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Sensitive auth/session fields are not written to logs.
- Production-safe default logging is enforced.
- Ops docs include temporary enable/disable steps and retention guidance.


"[Supply Chain][P2] Pin GitHub Actions to immutable commit SHAs"
## Summary
Workflows currently pin actions by tags/versions rather than full commit SHAs.

## Why
SHA pinning reduces supply-chain risk from compromised/moved tags.

## Scope
- Replace action tag references with audited commit SHA pins.
- Keep update process documented for future maintenance.

## Acceptance Criteria
- All third-party actions in repository workflows are pinned to full commit SHAs.
- README/CONTRIBUTING (or workflow comments) document how to safely bump pins.


"[Security][P2] Add CI secret-scanning gate for new commits"
## Summary
Add automated secret scanning to CI to prevent accidental credential leaks.

## Why
Public repos need continuous guardrails against token/key exposure.

## Scope
- Integrate a secret scanning tool in CI (e.g., gitleaks/trufflehog equivalent).
- Fail CI on verified leaks, with actionable output.
- Tune baseline/allowlist to avoid noisy false positives.

## Acceptance Criteria
- CI runs secret scan on PRs and/or pushes.
- Pipeline fails on real secret findings.
- Contributor guidance documents how to resolve findings.


"[Release Hygiene][P2] Add pre-public-release verification checklist for config/log secret hygiene"
## Summary
Formalize and automate checks ensuring sensitive runtime files are never committed.

## Why
Before flipping to public, release hygiene must include explicit checks for config and logs.

## Scope
- Verify and enforce ignore rules for config/config.php, .env*, logs/*.
- Add a documented pre-release checklist step for secret hygiene verification.
- Optionally add CI checks for forbidden tracked files.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Ignore rules are validated and documented.
- Pre-release checklist includes mandatory secret hygiene verification.
- CI or scripted check flags forbidden tracked sensitive files."
